# Environment files

When editing `.env`, `.env.local`, `.env.example`, or any env file:

- **Never overwrite the whole file** to add new variables
- **Never delete or blank out** existing variables
- **Only append or update** the specific keys you need to change
- Before writing, read the current file and **merge** new keys into the existing contents
- If a key already exists, update that line only; leave all other lines untouched

```text
# ❌ BAD — replaces the file and drops MONGODB_URI / other keys
write entire .env with only the new R2_* vars

# ✅ GOOD — read .env, keep every existing line, append or set only new keys
R2_ENDPOINT=...
```
